                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>It includes pharmacodynamics (pharmacology) and pharmacokinetics. Pharmacodynamics mainly studies the effects of drugs on the body (including pathogens) and their mechanisms of action to clarify the laws of drug treatment of diseases, providing a theoretical basis for guiding rational clinical drug use and reducing toxic and side effects; pharmacokinetics mainly studies the processes of drugs in the body (including absorption, distribution, metabolism and excretion), explaining the dynamic laws of drugs in the body, thereby determining the dosage and interval of administration, etc.</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
